# Byteman observation rule, cluster tier of group-by-limit-incrementGroupCount-groupLimit--autonomous (audit amendment A11). Observation only: it changes nothing.
# Loaded at node start with  -javaagent:<byteman.jar>=script:<this file>  -Dstage4.trace=<file>
# One line per local sub-page read of a GROUP BY query, written when the counter is closed (end of that read):
#   GB ms=<epoch ms> rows=<rowsCounted> groups=<groupCounted> unfinished=<hasUnfinishedGroup> done=<isDone()>
# rows = rows that passed the counter in this read (<= rowLimit = page size P); groups = groups completed in this read; done = groupCounted >= groupLimit
# (DataLimits.java:1013; the stop at :993-994 is the target). PagingGroupByAwareCounter inherits onClose, so continuation reads are traced as well.

RULE l79 groupby counter close
CLASS org.apache.cassandra.db.filter.DataLimits$CQLGroupByLimits$GroupByAwareCounter
METHOD onClose
AT EXIT
IF TRUE
DO traceOpen("l79", java.lang.System.getProperty("stage4.trace", "l79.trace"));
   traceln("l79", "GB ms=" + java.lang.System.currentTimeMillis() + " rows=" + $0.rowsCounted + " groups=" + $0.groupCounted + " unfinished=" + $0.hasUnfinishedGroup + " done=" + $0.isDone())
ENDRULE
